       "id": "REQ-cycle-repository-2",
       "kind": "reliability",
       "title": "Bounded transient recovery classification",
-      "statement": "Given a provider or chain attempt that fails before, during, or after an external effect, when the repository classifies its recovery path, then it assigns exactly one of three classes: semantic-invalid (the request itself is wrong and requires a terminal HELD_* state with an owner decision), effect-ambiguous (the external outcome cannot yet be distinguished and the attempt stays observation-only until canonical evidence resolves it), or proven-pre-effect-transient (no external effect occurred and the identical approved intent may retry automatically once the blocking condition clears). A Relay quote that expires before any request or signature is proven-pre-effect-transient: it stays nonterminal with no cycle terminal state and no attempt, persists the expired quote identity and deadline, and only after re-proving no signed or broadcast attempt exists does policy/admission atomically select one replacement quote for the same claimed principal under `refresh-after-readmission`; it never silently substitutes a quote once signed bytes exist. A Solana chain attempt whose blockhash expires past its validity boundary is effect-ambiguous: it stays `BROADCAST` and observation-only until reconciliation either finalizes it or produces canonical expired-and-unlanded proof, and only then creates exactly one linked replacement attempt with a fresh blockhash under `reconcile-then-replace`, retaining the original signed bytes and signature permanently. A wallet lease or fencing token lost strictly before the provider or signature capability boundary is proven-pre-effect-transient: it stays `NOT_SENT` with no cycle terminal state, and a newly fenced owner may retry the identical prepared request digest exactly once under `retry-same-request-under-new-lease`. Lease loss discovered after a provider-mutation capability boundary was already reached is a distinct, effect-ambiguous class: it is reclassified `SENT_UNKNOWN`, stays observation-only under `reconcile-before-retry`, and forbids any automatic retry or new provider mutation until canonical reconciliation resolves the prior attempt; it never shares the pre-boundary class's tuple. Lease loss discovered after a signing capability boundary was already reached is instead governed by the durable chain-attempt contract's own `PREPARED`/`SIGNED`/`BROADCAST`/`REFUSED` states from REQ-cycle-repository-1, not by `SENT_UNKNOWN`, because a chain attempt already carries its own state machine for that ambiguity. An external signer denial that provably occurred before any signature could have been produced is proven-pre-effect-transient: it stays `NOT_SENT` with no cycle terminal state, persists a bounded redacted signer-unavailable reason and next retry time, and retries the identical request against the same approved signer identity after bounded backoff under `retry-after-signer-readiness`. A sign-only external signer timeout may retry the identical signing attempt only for the verified owned Keychain broker, whose separate, distinctly guarded broadcast capability the checked-in source proves its sign operation never reaches. That retry is proven-pre-effect-transient only when the exact unsigned wire bytes, signer role/account identity, request digest, policy/authorization digest, and validity context were durably persisted before that broker's sign-only operation was first invoked; the retry reuses those exact durably bound values, never regenerates the provider transaction, blockhash, nonce, memo, or policy under the retry's identity, and never asserts the prior attempt produced no signature \u2014 a signature returned by either attempt is captured exactly once through the existing signed-bytes recovery record, which rejects materially different signing material, under `retry-sign-only-with-durable-binding`. This identical-byte, idempotent-retry guarantee is enabled only once focused evidence proves it for that exact broker contract; it grants no broadcast authority, and a subsequent broadcast or provider-send outcome that cannot be distinguished remains its own observation-only `SENT_UNKNOWN` or chain-attempt state, never retried as an unsigned request. Every opaque or external-module signer timeout keeps the existing no-automatic-retry, terminal whole-cycle class, because canonical chain observation cannot recover or rule out an unbroadcast signature for it; automatic sign-only retry is not extended to any other signer by this revision, and a future signer can receive it only through a later owner-approved spec revision bound to that exact signer contract, never by an implementation-time claim of equivalence. Edge case: a stale fenced owner performs no effect after fence failure; a class assignment never exports a key, substitutes a signer, or creates a new request; and semantic-invalid classes (wrong-asset, wrong-recipient, cross-cycle attribution failure, conflicting canonical evidence) keep their existing terminal HELD_* owner-decision contract unchanged.",
