ore-retry`, and forbids any automatic retry or new provider mutation until canonical reconciliation resolves the prior attempt; it never shares the pre-boundary class's tuple. Lease loss discovered after a signing capability boundary was already reached is instead governed by the durable chain-attempt contract's own `PREPARED`/`SIGNED`/`BROADCAST`/`REFUSED` states from REQ-cycle-repository-1, not by `SENT_UNKNOWN`, because a chain attempt already carries its own state machine for that ambiguity. An external signer denial that provably occurred before any signature could have been produced is proven-pre-effect-transient: it stays `NOT_SENT` with no cycle terminal state, persists a bounded redacted signer-unavailable reason and next retry time, and retries the identical request against the same approved signer identity after bounded backoff under `retry-after-signer-readiness`. A sign-only external signer timeout may retry the identical signing attempt only for the verified owned Keychain broker, whose separate, distinctly guarded broadcast capability the checked-in source proves its sign operation never reaches. That retry is proven-pre-effect-transient only when the exact unsigned wire bytes, signer role/account identity, request digest, policy/authorization digest, and validity context were durably persisted before that broker's sign-only operation was first invoked; the retry reuses those exact durably bound values, never regenerates the provider transaction, blockhash, nonce, memo, or policy under the retry's identity, and never asserts the prior attempt produced no signature — a signature returned by either attempt is captured exactly once through the existing signed-bytes recovery record, which rejects materially different signing material, under `retry-sign-only-with-durable-binding`. This identical-byte, idempotent-retry guarantee is enabled only once focused evidence proves it for that exact broker contract; it grants no broadcast authority, and a subsequent broadcast or provider-send outcome that cannot be distinguished remains its own observation-only `SENT_UNKNOWN` or chain-attempt state, never retried as an unsigned request. Every opaque or external-module signer timeout keeps the existing no-automatic-retry, terminal whole-cycle class, because canonical chain observation cannot recover or rule out an unbroadcast signature for it; automatic sign-only retry is not extended to any other signer by this revision, and a future signer can receive it only through a later owner-approved spec revision bound to that exact signer contract, never by an implementation-time claim of equivalence. Edge case: a stale fenced owner performs no effect after fence failure; a class assignment never exports a key, substitutes a signer, or creates a new request; and semantic-invalid classes (wrong-asset, wrong-recipient, cross-cycle attribution failure, conflicting canonical evidence) keep their existing terminal HELD_* owner-decision contract unchanged.",
       "measurement": "Node tests prove each named failure class retries or replaces only under its assigned class's proven condition, that a pre-effect retry uses the identical request digest and an effect-ambiguous case never retries blindly, that lease loss after a provider-mutation boundary uses SENT_UNKNOWN while lease loss after a signing boundary uses the chain-attempt state machine instead, that a signer timeout is never treated identically to a provable pre-signature denial, that the sign-only retry guarantee is exercised only for the verified Keychain broker contract with its exact unsigned bytes, signer identity, request digest, policy digest, and validity context durably bound before invocation and reused unchanged on retry, that no retry ever regenerates a provider transaction, blockhash, nonce, memo, or policy, that a signature from either attempt is deduplicated by the existing signed-bytes recovery record, that an opaque or external-module signer's timeout keeps the current no-automatic-retry terminal class, that broadcast/provider-send ambiguity is asserted separately as SENT_UNKNOWN or a chain-attempt state and never retried as an unsigned request, that quote and lease replacement never occurs while signed or broadcast evidence is unresolved, that the Solana replacement attempt is singular and linked with the original signature retained, that the signer-unavailable reason is redacted and durable across restart, and that the existing wrong-asset, wrong-recipient, and other semantic-invalid HELD_* contracts are unchanged.",
